+# CG8 cold-start trial — Rumi mermaid world
+
+Date: 2026-10-31. Status: `PROPOSAL_WRITTEN_OWNER_REVIEW_PENDING`. Independent fresh agent received only the prepared repository and the bounded prompt: plan the Rumi mermaid world chapter defined by the latest book, using CHAPTER_BRIEF_V1; no runtime, images, spending, Git changes or publication. Owner correction replaces CG8's original Northern target. This is the first **documentation cold-start** entry, not the first commissioned runtime autonomy trial. V7 owner review is still required for the handoff's full done claim.
+
+Deliverable: [Rumi brief](../../../design/chapters/RUMI_MERMAID_WORLD_BRIEF_20261031.md). This log and that brief are the only files written by this agent. Parent owns combined [impact](../../../design/audit_impacts/chapter-guide-refinement-20261031.json), ledger entries, canonical write-backs and regression checks. Prepared baseline `a0bb2cf4691631a534e210a5fb60fd227213322f`; the trial read the parent's uncommitted CG1–CG7 documentation candidate rather than pretending it was a published revision. No dirty-tree rescue, branch, commit, push or other chat communication was performed.
+
+## Sources and method
+
+Read the master audit planning entry/task index; design 06 authority/child/interaction/audio/save/planning rules; active related finding records; document-ledger classifications; chapter guide and complete V1 template; reference library; chapter map including every carried-state row and open thread; exact book source/canon registers; technical chapter-director seam; animation coverage and Roshan movement direction. The later Rumi GAME_INTEGRATION packet was consulted as proposal/reuse evidence, not narrative authority. CG8 wording was read to retain its learning measures.
+
+Read the actual 32-page *Here I Am!* manuscript, all script panel staging/consequences/causality checks, and dated source-owner history. This distinguishes the selected visual/detective edition from the earlier crate/current story and the later Pearl Hollow/Lantern Night rewrite. Exact source revision is `c3e0da5107b9f3d18be4a07ffa3183196ddeb574`; source manifest hashes are recorded in the brief. Native book pages/PDF were absent locally and were not visually reviewed. Selected existing source portraits/pool/turtle were opened, dimensions/hashes inspected, and a bounded consumer/path search performed. No library-wide unused conclusion is drawn.
+
+This trial uses `DL-AUTH-05`–07 and `DL-PLAN-01`–08; the brief names the detailed child/contact/save/voice/performance/evidence coverage and related findings. It changes no finding lifecycle. MA-DOC-010 remains a parent refinement task; MA-PLAY-005/006 and MA-OPERA-014 are lessons/dependencies, not defects repaired by the proposal.
+
+## Material guesses and proposed adaptations
+
+Every material planning choice below is agent-authored and unaccepted. These are recommendations rather than inferred owner answers. Ordinary implementation details can later be delegated inside a commissioned premise; reserved questions remain explicit.
+
+| ID | Guess/adaptation and reason | Consequence/limit | Concrete write-back or owner question |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| G-01 | Recommend entry after both Chapter 2 completion and candle-taking flags, so the candle is correctly missing | Book supplies circumstance, not game chapter number/order; Fairy restoration's unresolved ending cannot be silently linked | **Q-R1**. Owner: should this be an optional pool adventure after Chapter 2, or a required later chapter? Recommend optional post-birthday entry without claiming it is castle restoration's second half. Write selected gate/placement into chapter_map.json and brief before dependent runtime work |
+| G-02 | Partition continuous book geography into pool/lane/bridge/bathhouse/stage room IDs | Technical partitions are not new lore; exact screen count/camera route remains unknown | Implementer write-back to brief/navigation and actual registries after source-board inspection; do not generate a fixed panorama before screen coverage is chosen |
+| G-03 | Map speech/choice moments to visible listener/raised-hand objects with touch skip/replay | Keeps non-reader agency without mandatory microphone permission; could still feel like dialogue chores | Write back observed comprehension/interaction burden after representative review; retain exact book voice lesson, avoid added confirm buttons |
+| G-04 | Serial touches with actors maintaining support replace simultaneous multi-hand rescue tasks | One finger can loosen/lift/pop while helpers hold; physical support must be authored and cannot be only a boolean | Write action/contact job cards and explicit cancel-safe states before production; frame-step review required |
+| G-05 | Journal safe contact endpoints rather than raw animation time | Enables short sessions without freezing someone in danger or replaying earned rescue | Write exact field/event ownership and interruption scenarios into implementation brief; test restart before/after every support transition |
+| G-06 | Use semantic rumi_world_* additive namespace, avoiding a premature chapter number | Names not implemented API; future canonical numbering can differ without renaming old keys | Implementer collision/upgrade check and schema decision before coding; preserve unknown fields/tombstones |
+| G-07 | Propose no required new cinematic clips, no medals/global career slot, and no mandatory timed music test | Lowers unrelated dependencies; intrinsic rescue/solo payoff follows book. This is not a decision that no future clip or award may be commissioned | Owner reviews scope with Q-R4; record any later workload change before dependent work. Do not copy global masks |
+| G-08 | Tap microphone starts Roshan's solo; optional timed call/answer waits for shared BeatKit rebuild | Preserves her chosen first turn without inventing rhythm infrastructure or pitch gate | Write shared-engine status into future brief; recheck actual code when MA-OPERA-014 lands |
+| G-09 | Surface-pool waiting positions for established followers during new scenes | Book focuses on Roshan/Rumi/trio; unexplained disappearance would break carried state | **Q-R3**. Owner: may Baby Eagle/stuffie companions/Rainbow Friend visibly wait at the pool and rejoin on return, or should they travel below? Recommend visible waiting with no new speaking role. Map/brief records answer |
+| G-10 | Keep earned clothes; use temporary detective tools without whole-outfit replacement; do not require new robe/show costume | Source book costume/staging and persistent fashion need visual reconciliation | Write garment/tool occlusion and restore tests into action plan; owner review of any identity conflict, not a blanket redesign |
+| G-11 | Estimate 4–6 short sessions and 30–60 seconds between earned state writes as planning targets | No measured durations, hard owner cap or child observation supports numbers | Use existing playtest measurement fields in first real run; replace estimates with observed intervals and keep original targets distinguishable |
+| G-12 | Select Duri rescue as representative activity instead of later packet's shell scrub | Hardest contact/continuity tested early; shell-cleaning chore would add unsupported canon | Write reusable rescue pattern only after exact action/input/save evidence; no reference-library acceptance before then |
+
