+| F-04 | No verified game-ready Hana/Nari/Duri or complete fan/cloth/hook/wand action families | Both rescues and cast | After recovery, source/action coverage table with existing/gap/authority per state; profiles and job cards before bounded production. No new redesign merely to fill absent files |
+| F-05 | Only Roshan has a listed individual movement profile | Rumi/Hana/Nari/Duri/each imp | Animation register write-back: sourced profiles required for actual action production; this proposal does not create commission/biography |
+| F-06 | Source pool master inspected at 1672×941; book backgrounds' native per-screen coverage unknown | New playable screen coverage | Add source-dimensions/scene-grid evidence to future shortlist; existing pool reference does not satisfy 2048×2048 per playable screen rule |
+| F-07 | No Rumi production director/route/registry/probes; shared BeatKit/platform absent from tracked paths examined | All new implementation and optional rhythm | Recheck actual extension seam before commission; use typed RefCounted/main-owned state/SaveState, extend real registry gate. Record target-versus-built service status without making another framework |
+| F-08 | Fresh-save route proof not supplied by Chapter 2 fixture coverage | Entry acceptance | Keep MA-PLAY-005 scope open; required New Game route earns prerequisites with real touches before Rumi route. Parent does not claim source checks close reachability |
+| F-09 | No exact audio timing, required cue recordings, Mobile captures, device run or child observation | Pacing, performance, visual/voice/child acceptance | Named V4/V5/V6/V7 rows in brief stay PENDING. Use exact build/capture/APK and existing playtest fields; never turn estimates/scores into observed acceptance |
+| F-10 | Final chapter name/number, thread owner marks and acceptance ladder are provisional defaults except explicit October 31 corrections | Documentary aliases/status | Parent retain provisional labels; owner may answer existing naming/thread questions separately. Do not relabel code/save keys or infer more answers |
+| F-11 | Turtle concept's runtime approval/license is unresolved in proposal packet | Duri source choice | Source/license custodian verifies original source row and book selection before runtime derivation; no claim that concept membership is approval |
+| F-12 | Exact random/passive/repeat/cancel behavior of proposed controls and saved contradictory/future states is unimplemented | Safety/compatibility | Future implementation acceptance lists real input negatives and primary/backup/upgrades. Unknown raw data preserved; no malformed save may fabricate completion or destroy earned facts |
+
+## Canon conflicts caught and retained
+
+| ID | Conflict/risk found | Resolution in proposal | Concrete write-back |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C-01 | Newer GAME_INTEGRATION/WORLD_BIBLE presents Pearl Hollow/Lantern Night, Boom Shell, new citizens and five-room mystery as a coherent alternative | Exact selected book wins; exclude those plot substitutions, lantern tasks and shell scrub | BOOK_SOURCES already names BGM-01–06; keep its warning adjacent to later packet route. Future revision handoff must visibly link selected authority |
+| C-02 | Later packet turns glint into an entrance/clue; selected book proves reflected light then stows both tools | Dive is through existing pool opening; light test reveals no candle/object/door | Bind R02 to shade/unshade/stow and source p3; a future canon test/checklist must reject candle-recovery or glint-door completion |
+| C-03 | Older history contains crates/current clearing, later packet whirlpool/lantern mechanics; latest book uses fan base/bag loop, help and active backward escape | One fan with supported base, distinct bag strap/tie; no crate inventory or magic-song lifting | Source action table/job cards cite p8–12 staging, not earlier summary |
+| C-04 | Rumi speaks in book, existing Chapter 2 scope forbids invented Rumi performance | Plan book dialogue; preserve existing restriction on unauthorized runtime voice | CANON-C02/OQ-RUMI-RUNTIME-VOICE and Q-R2; book-first does not authorize voice likeness |
+| C-05 | Magician bubble rescue can become a generic imp boss defeat or premature pop | Support with cloth/low platform, fixed hook, Rumi's retrieved wand, short safe landing; practical amends and shared turns | Future negative control rejects pop before support/hook; human support/contact review remains blocking |
+| C-06 | Book's still-missing candle could be mistaken for new clue/restoration ending/Ember continuation | No location/idea content revealed at home; no restoration linkage or new kinship | Chapter map open threads retained, Q-R1 decides placement only |
+| C-07 | Persistent outfits/followers absent from book panels could be stripped/forgotten by literal adaptation | Preserve earned state; bounded staging proposal flagged, no membership removal | Q-R3 and future fashion/return test plan |
+
+No canon contradiction was knowingly introduced into the selected-book plot. That statement is a static proposal review, not proof that owner/child will accept the adaptation. No founding August 30 wording is re-attributed beyond the spine's recorded incorporation summary; parent retains the distinct source-history gap.
+
+Completion reconciliation: parent surfaced the current `ODR-DEMO-FREEZE-20261031` and the conditional Grand Puff care-recast decision `ODR-DEMO-GRAND-PUFF-20261031` / CANON-C16. The brief explicitly retains the gameplay freeze as another boundary on any future commission, and leaves the separate Grand Puff mismatch unresolved rather than treating older dirt canon as sole owner intent. Concrete write-back: keep CANON-C16/source-recovery pointer current in the canon register; no Rumi plot rewrite or runtime action depends on resolving it in this documentation trial. These are repository-authority updates supplied during the parent review, not fresh owner answers to Q-R1–Q-R4.
+
+## Duplicated-system risks
+
+| ID | Risk | Reuse boundary and concrete write-back |
+|---|---|---|
+| D-01 | Creating a second progression singleton/save document/director framework | Use current typed RefCounted/main-owned state, hook_event, serialize/restore/normalise and SaveState. Add bounded namespace and real calls, not aspirational platform APIs. Future technical touch list cites design 03 |
+| D-02 | Copying global career mask/medal identities into Rumi progress | Separate story journal/replay; preserve OPERA_ACTIVE_STAR_MASK and retired slots; no new career slot. Add compatibility negatives in eventual implementation |
+| D-03 | New beat clock/judge because later packet calls Rainbow Band an engine | Recheck actual rebuild; optional rhythm consumes landed shared service. Required book-first solo needs only intentional start and recorded answer, no cloned BeatKit |
+| D-04 | Separate touch/reward/audio lifecycle or callback-triggered completion | Inspect existing gesture ownership/AudioDirector, cancel on leave/focus loss, idempotent contact events. Add real production input and second-finger/stale-callback controls |
+| D-05 | Treating existing Chapter 2 own-room gate as certification for new steps | Extend gate to actual Rumi constructor registries with unbound/other-room faults; no all-room union or probe-only phase action |
+| D-06 | New library/book-reader, collection economy or outfit gates bundled into chapter | Excluded; only separately commissioned additions may enter future scope. Do not let attractive unused art add systems without player purpose |
+
+## Clarifications and successful reusable patterns
+
+No new owner answer was requested or received during the trial. Clarifications resolved from repository evidence: exact book selection; book-first narrative precedence; planning-only commission; semantic room aliases versus saved IDs; main-owned director state; source-art/voice acceptance separation; target architecture versus built APIs; V1 brief and first documentation trial versus runtime autonomy trial. Remaining reserved decisions are Q-R1–Q-R4, not guesses presented as facts.
+
+| Pattern | Evidence and successful use in this static trial | Concrete write-back / limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| Single front door for source choice | Master → map/canon/BOOK_SOURCES led directly to exact manuscript, staging and immutable hashes | Retain exact-source register; add native-art availability pointer F-03. Successful discovery, no art acceptance |
+| Newer proposal warning | Source register explicitly distinguishes Lantern Night rewrite from latest authored book | Keep warning in chapter recipe/reference shelf and ensure packet self-links back; prevented a material wrong-story plan |
+| Causal story/navigation/save tables | V1 fields exposed glint-door, support, ordinary-choice and return-state risks before coding | Keep these tables; add timing observations only after play, never use eight-job formula as universal template |
+| Own-room and fresh-save requirements | Guide's three checks forced every step toward actual objects and rejected fixture-based route claims | Future Rumi gate/route mutation evidence required; static plan is not acceptance |
+| Hard representative action | Choosing support/loosen/help/free exercises biggest uncertainty first | Promote only exact reviewed rescue pattern later, with action/contact/save limits |
+| Existing-service availability check | Tracked-path search found no BeatKit/platform implementation, while current directors/gesture/fashion/audio exist | Maintain built/proposed service distinction at fresh implementation head; no duplicated framework |
+| Acceptance ladder with separate columns | PLANNED is justified by proposal; commission/runtime/device/owner acceptance remain independent | CG8 log-exists criterion met; owner review remains open. No runtime autonomy-trial completion inferred |
+
+## Concrete parent write-back queue and result
+
+1. Add both exact file paths to the parent impact/ledger and link this trial from guide/map/reference navigation; run combined authority/development checks. Agent intentionally did not edit other files.
+2. Maintain BOOK_SOURCES' BGM-01–06 reconciliation and exact text hashes; add a native-art/manifests availability pointer after F-03 recovery. Do not promote the later revision packet as controlling narrative.
+3. Carry Q-R1 placement, Q-R2 voices, Q-R3 companion staging and Q-R4 implementation scope to owner review of the proposal. One question may refer to an existing owner-question ID; avoid duplicated contradictory decision records.
+4. Before actual implementation, convert proposal IDs/field names into real registry/save/contact contracts, recheck shared-engine state and source rights, and bind the representative rescue to actual input/negative/restart evidence.
+5. Keep CG8 owner review and the later commissioned runtime trial open. No runtime, art, device, child, release or finding acceptance follows from this static receipt.
+
+Implemented by trial: two proposal/log Markdown documents only. Machine verification: exact source text SHA-256 compared to SOURCES.json; shortlisted dimensions/hashes and known consumer paths inspected. Parent gates are separate pending results. Outstanding: owner proposal review and every runtime/visual/audio/device/child/product acceptance lane. No engine/probe run, image generation, spending, Git mutation or publication occurred.
+
+
+## Parent write-backs after trial review
+
+The parent added this log and the brief to the impact/ledger and routes the map/reference library to them. Existing BOOK_SOURCES/SOURCES.json now retain an immutable selected-art manifest link and exact availability limit. Q-R1 maps to OQ-RUMI-PLACEMENT, Q-R2 to OQ-RUMI-RUNTIME-VOICE, and Q-R4 to OQ-RUMI-CHAPTER-COMMISSION in the canon question register. Q-R3 is retained as an optional review preference: follower staging inside an approved premise is delegated, so waiting-position review must not become a new routine owner gate. Any new role/voice or material continuity change remains reserved. The architecture contract now explicitly allows a documented stable semantic save namespace while a chapter number is unset, preserving the additive-save rule and avoiding future renames.
