+# Book source authority
+
+Status: `BINDING_DOMAIN` for exact book-source selection and book/game precedence under DL-PLAN-08. A book's narrative authority is separate from art, voice, runtime, print, device, child and owner acceptance.
+
+## Owner correction — 2026-10-31
+
+The owner answered the chapter-guide handoff's Q3 and Q5 in the implementation chat:
+
+> 3 - book wins when it comes to mismatches, and the game needs to be re-written for the book. Also, let's not use the winter world as our first use of this tool, let's use the rumi mermaid world that's defined by the latest book.
+
+Recorded as ODR-BOOK-FIRST-20261031 and ODR-RUMI-CHAPTER-TRIAL-20261031. This replaces the handoff's game-first default and Northern trial target. Book precedence covers established story, world, cast and demonstrated identity/action mismatches; current game code or atlas wording cannot silently overrule the selected book. Preserve source originals and record the actual game adaptation rather than inventing an unobserved discrepancy. Chapter naming, reserved-thread marks and the acceptance ladder retain their explicitly provisional defaults; no new owner answer is inferred for those questions. This task commissions a planning trial, not gameplay or new book art.
+
+## Exact current Rumi source
+
+The latest illustrated source identified by the book handoff is *Mermaid Roshan: Here I Am!*, the visual/detective edition. Its narrative remains an owner-review candidate; the owner now directs this book's world as the planning source. The byte-identical [script](book_sources/rumi_visual_detective_20261012.json), [read-aloud manuscript](book_sources/rumi_visual_detective_20261012.txt), and [dated source-owner history](book_sources/rumi_owner_history_20261012.txt) are available on the reference shelf, with original paths, immutable revision and SHA-256 in [SOURCES.json](book_sources/SOURCES.json).
+
+Original source tree: [c3e0da51 book sources](https://github.com/Ebonyks/mermaid-roshan-reef/tree/c3e0da5107b9f3d18be4a07ffa3183196ddeb574/assets_src/books/rumi_visual_detective_20261012). Only text is copied here; selected artwork, earlier editions, native sources and PDFs stay preserved at their original revision. No source pixels or recorded voices change.
+
+The October 17/18 [revision handoff](../../docs/handoffs/codex_rumi_book_revision_2026-10-17/README.md) proposes Pearl Hollow, Lantern Night, a five-room bathhouse and Boom Shell. Its newer document date does not make that proposed rewrite the latest authored book. Do not replace the book's Song Night, fan/current rescue, extravagant feast, foam/bubble confrontation or voice lesson with that proposal unless the owner selects the replacement story.
+
+## Native-art availability
+
+The [immutable selected-art manifest](https://github.com/Ebonyks/mermaid-roshan-reef/blob/c3e0da5107b9f3d18be4a07ffa3183196ddeb574/assets_src/books/rumi_visual_detective_20261012/selected_art.json) has SHA-256 f3492f5eebeca5c29306e7e99ed7bec29c98d599f7177f3a3a43af64670d570f at the source revision. It names the existing selected native pages; those binaries are not copied into this documentation task. Recover and inspect them before declaring an action state absent or generating replacement artwork. The source-owner history records a FAIL regression result for the source book iteration; this task imports text only and neither imports its runtime state nor overwrites that failure with current game results.
+
+## Book-to-game reconciliation queue
+
+| ID | Book source and fact | Current game/source mismatch | Required adaptation / evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| BGM-01 | p2–3: Roshan wants her first line; detective hat/lens test proves a rainbow glint is light; candle remains missing | No under-pool chapter route or that investigation exists | Proposal names real world objects and an intentional observation test; implementation waits for a scoped chapter commission |
+| BGM-02 | p4–14: connected under-pool neighbourhood, trio, courier Duri, fan/cloth/current rescue | Current Mermaid Pool does not contain the book's city or rescue | Build geography and physical support/contact from book beats; inventory source art and code before generation |
+| BGM-03 | p15–17: heard comfort choices, bathhouse and extravagant couch feast; imps interrupt | Later handoff proposes a different bathhouse investigation and lantern mystery | Adapt the book's respite/relationships; additional world detail may support them only within approved boundaries |
+| BGM-04 | p18–29: foam/bubble stage action, speaking up, deliberate shared physical help and practical amends | Later proposal substitutes Boom Shell/whistle mechanics | Preserve the book's causality; one-finger controls and saved milestones require separate implementation and contact review |
+| BGM-05 | p30–32: Roshan's chosen solo first line, ensemble answer, ordinary idea at home; Rumi has dialogue | Existing Chapter 2 uses Rumi animation/notes with no invented runtime voice | Book dialogue is narrative authority; it grants no new voice likeness or recording rights. Plan exact cues and record missing performance/owner voice choice |
+| BGM-06 | Source book includes Rumi, Hana and Nari as the trio, with Roshan protagonist; no Kareem and no candle recovery | Agent proposal names extra citizens, kinship and different finale premises | Keep new source-book characters PLANNED for runtime; exclude proposal-only characters from active canon; leave kinship/candle extensions reserved |
+
+These are planning mismatches, not newly reproduced runtime defects. Link a commissioned game's impact and relevant existing finding when work begins. Do not claim this queue already repairs the game or accepts the book.
