+# Mermaid Roshan and the Song Beneath the Pool
+
+Status: `OWNER_COMMISSIONED_BOOK_DRAFT`; agent-authored story and character candidates, not accepted runtime or final print art.
+
+## Commission and boundaries
+
+On 2026-10-09 the owner approved the under-pool Korean mermaid-city concept and requested: "Looks great, draw the whole book. We should design two new mermaids based off of the characters here as well as a part of the story. Feel free to make new names for them". The supplied `kpop.jpg` supplies broad tall-redhead/younger-performer archetypes; new designs do not reproduce the film's characters, clothing, weapons, lore or songs.
+
+This explicitly commissions new illustrations for this new story. It does not reopen redraws of the existing picture-book adaptation under `DL-ASSET-08`. Existing books, Grok selections, family art and voices stay intact. Everything happens in Pearl Castle: the Korean mermaid city is beneath Rumi's pool, whose magic already exists. No Kareem; no candle recovery or change to the Ember King's motive. The separately implemented Fairy Conservatory route remains its own scoped source.
+
+On 2026-10-10 the owner requests refinement to 32 pages and substantially more comic content. The first draft remains preserved at its original paths: it had 576 story words on 19 PDF sheets, with 34 logical page labels. The revision uses exactly 32 actual PDF pages, including cover and illustrated back. The owner accepts the comic direction; this does not imply approval of every new frame or final print production.
+
+The owner's next2026-10-10 instruction commissions iterative page/design-language review, a bathhouse scene and interrupted couch downtime using broad K-Pop Demon Hunters tropes. This source-book iteration revises pages15-17: vulnerable relief after the rescue, a towel joke, friends making couch space for Duri, a quiet shared snack/song and the existing imps' showy entrance. The actual prior pages and native sources were viewed first. Original dialogue and staging preserve the cast, under-pool setting and three-crate causality; no film shots, lyrics, character designs, weapons or lore are reproduced. Quiet mint/cream backgrounds, differentiated expressions and sequential panels address repeated smiling crops and dense equal-value dressing. [Iteration impact](../audit_impacts/rumi-bathhouse-iteration-20261010.json).
+
+The owner correction 2026-10-11 rejects the prior page framing: "table with food needs to be much larger and more extravagant" and "it should look more like manga", with big awkward boxes and too much whitespace. The new manga-feast iteration replaces the rounded-card/external-lettering-band system throughout the book, using tighter square frames, varied source-specific panels, meaningful reaction/detail crops and compact in-art captions/balloons. Two targeted foreground table/food edits carry the same extravagant banquet through pages 16-17; the couch, cast, bathhouse, interruption and plot are retained. Earlier editions are historical review sources, not evidence that the rejected layout was accepted. [Manga-feast impact](../audit_impacts/rumi-manga-feast-20261011.json).
+
+## Owner correction: sustained action - 2026-10-11
+
+The owner rejects the plot density of the manga-feast edition: "The plot is also far, far too thin to support this much material, there should be 1-2 detailed action sequences as well". This commissions a story rewrite within the existing under-pool premise, rather than treating more crops or more panels as plot. The new source is `assets_src/books/rumi_action_story_20261011/story_script.json`, with a complete page/panel [manuscript](../../assets_src/books/rumi_action_story_20261011/MANUSCRIPT.txt) and a clearly labelled 32-page story-script proof. The illustrated manga-feast edition remains a historical layout/art review source; it does not depict the new action states. [Story-action impact](../audit_impacts/rumi-action-story-20261011.json).
+
+Roshan wants a place in the neighbourhood's evening song but believes her little voice may not count. The imps' oversized show props block the existing song current and trap the courier who carries the invitations. Roshan's listening leads to a difficult rescue; sharing the load lets the group succeed. At the stage, the same obstruction becomes a defended physical problem. The saved courier's experience then helps Roshan after her own straight pull fails. The restored current lets Duri complete his real delivery, and Roshan sings before deliberately leaving a space for the city to answer. The missing candle stays unresolved.
+
+| Pages | Story purpose and sustained action |
+|---|---|
+| 2-8 | Set personal desire, connected city geography, tram pulses/current-following, Duri's overloaded delivery, trio personalities, the song/listening gap and missing city answer. |
