+PAGE 01 - Mermaid Roshan: Here I Am!
+
+[p01.1]
+Title: Mermaid Roshan: Here I Am!
+Subtitle: An adventure beneath Rumi's pool
+
+PAGE 02 - A turn, and a little glint
+
+[p02.1]
+Narrator: The castle candle was still missing. But tonight, a song was waiting beneath Rumi's pool.
+Roshan: I want to sing the first line. All by myself.
+
+[p02.2]
+Rumi: Then let's make that your turn.
+Roshan: What if my voice wobbles?
+Rumi: It can wobble. It's still yours. I'll be beside you, if you want.
+
+[p02.3]
+Roshan: Is that a rainbow under the bench?
+
+[p02.4]
+Roshan: My detective hat!
+
+[p02.5]
+Roshan: Too low.
+
+[p02.6]
+Roshan: Now I can see.
+
+PAGE 03 - Looking before guessing
+
+[p03.1]
+Roshan: I'll look before I guess.
+
+[p03.2]
+Roshan: Could our candle be here?
+
+[p03.3]
+Roshan: Can you watch the glint?
+Rumi: Yes.
+
+[p03.4]
+Rumi: It's moving with the rainbow.
+
+[p03.5]
+Roshan: It's light. There's no candle under here.
+
+[p03.6]
+Rumi: Ready for Song Night?
+Roshan: Yes. And I still want my first line.
+
+PAGE 04 - The neighbourhood and the warning
+
+[p04.1]
+Narrator: Under the pool lay a whole neighbourhood. Tonight, everyone would sing together.
+Narrator: The baker packed warm snacks. The tailor hung bright ribbons. Everyone had a song to bring.
+
+[p04.2]
+Duri: Song Night! Bring your own voice! One last invitation for the bathhouse. Then I get a turn too!
+Rumi: The lanterns go up. The singing begins.
+
+[p04.3]
+Rumi: Stay beside me under the bridge. The tram stirs a strong current.
+
+[p04.4]
+Performer: Our entrance will be HUGE!
+Duri: That fan is hanging over my delivery path.
+
+[p04.5]
+Magician: We'll move it later. Come and clap!
+Duri: But I need to get through now.
+
+PAGE 05 - Everybody has an idea
+
+[p05.1]
+Rumi: Hana dances. Nari keeps the beat. Tonight, Roshan wants...
+
+[p05.2]
+Hana: A giant finish!
+Nari: And a booming beginning!
+
+[p05.3]
+Roshan: I wanted...
+Hana: Rumi first, then all of us!
+
+PAGE 06 - The swallowed sentence
+
+[p06.1]
+Roshan: Could I sing the...
+Narrator: She had practised her three words all morning. She wanted them to be heard.
+
+[p06.2]
+Sound: BOOM!
+Narrator: The end of her sentence disappeared.
+
+[p06.3]
+Duri, off-panel: Help!
+Roshan: That wasn't part of the song.
+
+PAGE 07 - Wait for me
+
+[p07.1]
+Roshan: Wait! Someone needs help!
+
+[p07.2]
+Hana: I thought that was an echo.
+Roshan: I heard it twice. Please come and look.
+
+[p07.3]
+Rumi: We're coming.
+Narrator: This time, Roshan finished her sentence.
+
+PAGE 08 - Under the bridge
+
+[p08.1]
+Duri: Down here!
+
+[p08.2]
+Duri: The fan slipped. My bag is caught, and I can't back out.
+Rumi: We'll go one step at a time.
+
+[p08.3]
+Hana: I can pull it up!
+Duri: Wait. That tugs my bag!
+
+PAGE 09 - Stop means stop
+
+[p09.1]
+Roshan: Stop!
+
+[p09.2]
+Roshan: Hana. Stop pulling. Duri asked us to wait.
+
+[p09.3]
+Hana: I'm stopping. Tell us what you need.
+Duri: Loosen my bag first. Please.
+
+PAGE 10 - The little loop
+
+[p10.1]
+Duri: Push the fan back a little. That will loosen the loop.
+
+[p10.2]
+Rumi: I'll hold this edge. Hana, keep it steady.
+
+[p10.3]
+Roshan: Loose... and off!
+
+PAGE 11 - A stronger rush
+
+[p11.1]
+Nari: Another tram! Hold on!
+
+[p11.2]
+Narrator: WHOOSH! The fan pushed back.
+
+[p11.3]
+Roshan: Rumi, I need help at this end!
+Rumi: Coming beside you.
+
+PAGE 12 - One move together
+
+[p12.1]
+Nari: Ready... now!
+
+[p12.2]
+Roshan: Back this way, Duri. We've got it.
+
+[p12.3]
+Narrator: Four flippers wriggled. One turtle was free!
+
+PAGE 13 - Heard at last
+
+[p13.1]
+Duri: I told those imps the path was blocked. They just kept talking.
+
+[p13.2]
+Roshan: My voice shook when I shouted.
+Hana: I'm glad you told me to stop. I thought being strong would help. I should have asked first.
+
+[p13.3]
+Duri: Can we rest before we go to the show?
+Rumi: Yes. The bathhouse is right here.
+
+PAGE 14 - Warm water, true words
+
+[p14.1]
+Narrator: In the warm bathhouse, Roshan found another sentence.
+
+[p14.2]
+Roshan: I wanted a turn in the song. You all kept talking.
+
+[p14.3]
+Rumi: We did. I promised you a turn, then forgot to make room. I'm sorry.
+Hana: I chose the song before you could choose.
+Nari: And my drum was louder than you.
+
+PAGE 15 - Little things count
+
+[p15.1]
+Roshan: Can we sit in the cooler pool?
+Rumi: Of course.
+
+[p15.2]
+Hana: Would you like a towel?
+Roshan: Not on my head, please.
+
+[p15.3]
+Hana: All right. I'll put it beside you instead.
+Nari: Then I'll wear enough for two! I am the queen of rabbits!
+
+PAGE 16 - She gets to choose
+
+[p16.1]
+Hana: What would you like your first line to be?
+
+[p16.2]
+Roshan: Here I am!
+Nari: Here you are!
+
+[p16.3]
+Roshan: Can we try it again at supper?
+Rumi: As many times as you like. We'll each have a turn.
+
+PAGE 17 - A feast and a beginning
+
+[p17.1]
+Narrator: Supper filled a table almost as long as the couch.
+
+[p17.2]
+Duri: A fruit mountain! I'll start at the bottom.
+Roshan: Can I start our song now?
+Hana: We're listening.
+
+[p17.3]
+Roshan, singing: Here I...
+
+PAGE 18 - The loud interruption
+
+[p18.1]
+Performer: SHOWTIME!
+
+[p18.2]
+Roshan: Your fan trapped Duri. You need to hear him.
+Hana: He's right here. Let him tell you.
+
+[p18.3]
+Magician: Later, little voice. Tonight, WE sing. You clap!
+
+PAGE 19 - I am speaking
+
+[p19.1]
+Roshan: I am speaking. Please listen. This is everyone's song. My friends have something to sing. And I do too.
+
+[p19.2]
+Performer: If we stop, they might forget us!
+
+[p19.3]
+Rumi: Roshan has a turn too.
+Nari: We can all fit in one song.
+
+PAGE 20 - The curtain goes up
+
+[p20.1]
+Magician: Then watch our BIGGEST trick!
+Narrator: With a tap of his wand, he popped a stray bubble.
+
+[p20.2]
+Narrator: Bubbles bulged. Foam stars flew. Nobody could reach the microphone.
+
+[p20.3]
+Roshan: I need you beside me. Let's keep a way through.
+
+PAGE 21 - The friends make a plan
+
+[p21.1]
+Rumi: This way, everyone. I'll keep the aisle open.
+
+[p21.2]
+Hana: I'll catch the stars.
+Nari: I'll give us a swimming beat.
+
+[p21.3]
+Duri: Last delivery! Now I can help.
+Roshan: I'll go through the gaps. Duri, ring if the path closes.
+
+PAGE 22 - A beat to swim by
+
+[p22.1]
+Trio, singing: Hold a beat. Leave a space.
+
+[p22.2]
+Trio, singing: Help each friend to find their place.
+
+[p22.3]
+Hana: Caught it!
+Nari: And duck!
+
+PAGE 23 - Change the way
+
+[p23.1]
+Performer: You're missing our grand finish!
+
+[p23.2]
+Sound: DING!
+Roshan: Pause! I need a different way.
+Hana: Give us a turn. We'll watch yours too.
+
+[p23.3]
+Roshan: The current goes under. Rumi, come with me.
+
+PAGE 24 - Under and around
+
+[p24.1]
+Narrator: Under the bubbles. Around the curtain. Together!
+
+[p24.2]
+Hana: Stars in the basket!
+Nari: Space on the stage!
+
+[p24.3]
+Magician: Nobody can miss THIS!
+
+PAGE 25 - The trick goes wrong
+
+[p25.1]
+Narrator: The tassel snagged. The wand slipped.
+
+[p25.2]
+Magician: Oh! This isn't the trick! Where's my wand? I can't reach it!
+
+[p25.3]
+Magician: Help!
+Narrator: His friend was still bowing.
+Performer: Ta-daaa!
+
+PAGE 26 - Somebody needs help
+
+[p26.1]
+Roshan: He's waving. He needs help!
+
+[p26.2]
+Roshan: Stop the show! Listen to him!
+Narrator: This time, nobody told her to wait.
+
+[p26.3]
+Magician: I can't get out.
+Roshan: We hear you. We're here. We won't leave you.
+
+PAGE 27 - Hold, then pop
+
+[p27.1]
+Roshan: Catch the bubble in the cloth!
+Performer: What can I do?
+Roshan: Tie back the curtain!
+
+[p27.2]
+Rumi: Ready below?
+Hana: Ready!
+
+[p27.3]
+Sound: POP!
+Magician: Oof. Thank you.
+
+PAGE 28 - Now they listen
+
+[p28.1]
+Magician: I called and called. Nobody heard me.
+
+[p28.2]
+Duri: That was how I felt under the bridge.
+Roshan: And when you talked over me.
+
+[p28.3]
+Magician: I'm sorry. We should have listened.
+Performer: I'm sorry I talked over you. I was afraid nobody would clap.
+Roshan: I was afraid too. I still wanted a turn.
+
+PAGE 29 - Room means doing something
+
+[p29.1]
+Narrator: They packed away the trick and opened the stage to everyone.
+
+[p29.2]
+Magician: After the song, we'll collect our fan.
+Duri: I'll show you the safe way to carry it.
+
+[p29.3]
+Roshan: I want the first line. Then you can have your turn.
+Performer: All right. We're listening.
+
+PAGE 30 - Here I am!
+
+[p30.1]
+Narrator: Her voice wobbled a little. She sang anyway.
+Roshan, singing: Here I am!
+
+[p30.2]
+Rumi, Hana and Nari, singing: Here you are!
+
+[p30.3]
+Everyone, singing: Near or far, big or small, we make room for us all!
+
+PAGE 31 - A turn is a turn
+
+[p31.1]
+Narrator: The imps had a turn. Then the neighbours did. Nobody had to steal the song.
+
+[p31.2]
+Duri: My deliveries are done. My turn to sing!
+
+[p31.3]
+Nari: Another line?
+Roshan: Yes. And then one of yours.
+
+PAGE 32 - A place at home
+
+[p32.1]
+Narrator: They swam back up through Rumi's pool. The rainbow was still turning.
+
+[p32.2]
+Rumi: What shall we do tomorrow?
+Roshan: I have an idea about our candle. Can I tell you?
+
+[p32.3]
+Rumi: I'm listening.
+Narrator: Roshan didn't wait for her voice to be perfect. She began.
+
